### Learning Management System API Tests
### Base URL
@baseUrl = http://localhost:5000
@token = your_jwt_token_here

### ============ AUTH ENDPOINTS ============

### 1. Register User
POST http://localhost:3000/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "litu@example.com",
  "password": "password123",
  "name": "Litu"
}

### 2. Register Another User (Instructor)
POST http://localhost:3000/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "instructor@example.com",
  "password": "password456",
  "name": "Jane Smith"
}

### 3. Login User
POST http://localhost:3000/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "litu@example.com",
  "password": "password123"
}

### 4. Get Profile (Requires Token)
GET http://localhost:3000/api/auth/profile
Authorization: Bearer eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9.eyJpZCI6IjJlNmMzZGYxLTZkNjUtNGE4ZC04OTJiLTQxMzQwNjU3OTc5NyIsImVtYWlsIjoibGl0dUBleGFtcGxlLmNvbSIsImlhdCI6MTc5MTIzMjc0MywiZXhwIjoxNzkxODM3NTQzfQ.C0zPK2ezr2PfUaF8QZXtE31ANTqySaw2B9yZ-WsnlM8

### ============ COURSE ENDPOINTS ============

### 5. Get All Courses
GET http://localhost:3000/api/courses

### 6. Get Course by ID
GET http://localhost:3000/api/courses/e96856b5-a4a0-408d-aba3-7d915458e66b

### 7. Create Course (Requires Token)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/courses
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "title": "Introduction to Web Development",
  "description": "Learn HTML, CSS, and JavaScript basics",
  "instructor_id": 1
}

### 8. Create Another Course
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/courses
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "title": "Advanced React.js",
  "description": "Master React hooks, context, and state management",
  "instructor_id": 1
}

### 9. Create Third Course
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/courses
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "title": "Node.js Backend Development",
  "description": "Build scalable APIs with Node.js and Express",
  "instructor_id": 2
}

### 10. Update Course (Requires Token)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/courses/1
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "title": "Introduction to Web Development - Updated",
  "description": "Learn HTML, CSS, JavaScript, and modern web development"
}

### 11. Delete Course (Requires Token)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/courses/3
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### ============ PROGRESS ENDPOINTS ============

### 12. Get User Progress (Requires Token)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/progress/user/1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 13. Get Progress for Specific Course (Requires Token)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/progress/user/1/course/1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 14. Update Progress - Start Course (Requires Token)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/progress/user/1/course/1
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "completed_lessons": 2,
  "completion_percentage": 25
}

### 15. Update Progress - Midway (Requires Token)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/progress/user/1/course/1
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "completed_lessons": 5,
  "completion_percentage": 50
}

### 16. Update Progress - Complete Course (Requires Token)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/progress/user/1/course/1
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "completed_lessons": 10,
  "completion_percentage": 100
}

### 17. Update Progress for Another Course (Requires Token)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/progress/user/1/course/2
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "completed_lessons": 3,
  "completion_percentage": 15
}

### 18. Delete Progress (Requires Token)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/progress/user/1/course/2
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 19. Get All Progress for User 2 (Requires Token)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/progress/user/2
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### ============ HEALTH CHECK ============

### 20. Health Check
GET {{baseUrl}}/health

### ============ QUICK TEST FLOW ============
### Run these in order to test the full workflow:

# Step 1: Register a user
# Step 2: Login to get token
# Step 3: Copy token and replace {{token}} variable
# Step 4: Create courses
# Step 5: Update progress
# Step 6: Get progress

### Notes:
### - Replace {{token}} with actual JWT token from login response
### - User ID is returned after successful login (check response)
### - Instructor ID should match a user ID in the database
### - Course ID is returned after course creation
